# Environment variables

The service is configured by environment variables only; `server serve`
and `server worker` read the same ones. Values are checked at startup, and a
missing required value stops the process with a message that names it.

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `APP_ENV` | `development` | Deployment name; `production` refuses unsafe settings |
| `GRPC_ADDR` | `:10000` | gRPC listen address (`serve`) |
| `HTTP_ADDR` | `:8080` | REST and `/livez`, `/readyz` (`serve`) |
| `ADMIN_ADDR` | | Admin port, for example `:9090`: `/readyz` with details, `/version`, `/metrics` (Prometheus), `/debug/pprof/`. Keep it private. The worker serves its probes only here |
| `GRPC_REFLECTION` | `false` | gRPC server reflection (authenticated like other methods) |
| `SHUTDOWN_DELAY` | `5s` | Time to keep serving after readiness turns off |
| `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` | `30s` | Total graceful shutdown budget |
| `TRUSTED_PROXIES` | | Comma-separated CIDRs of the proxies in front of the service (client IP for rate limits) |
| `ERROR_DOMAIN` | `notify` | `ErrorInfo.domain` of API errors |
| `AUTH_ISSUER` | (required) | JWT issuer (`iss`) |
| `AUTH_JWKS_URL` | (required) | Issuer key set; https only (http for localhost) |
| `AUTH_AUDIENCE` | (required) | This service's audience (`aud`) |
| `AUTH_TOKEN_TYPES` | | Accepted JWT `typ` values, for example `at+jwt` |
| `AUTH_DISABLED` | `false` | Turn auth off; refused when `APP_ENV=production` |
| `PUBSUB_BROKERS` | (required) | Comma-separated seed brokers, `host:port` |
| `PUBSUB_TLS` | `true` | TLS to the brokers; `false` only for a local broker |
| `PUBSUB_ITEMS_TOPIC` | `notify-items` | Topic of the ItemCreated events |
| `PUBSUB_ITEMS_SUBSCRIPTION` | `notify-items-worker` | Consumer group of the worker |
| `PUBSUB_MAX_DELIVERY_ATTEMPTS` | `5` | Deliveries before a message goes to the dead-letter topic |
| `PUBSUB_ITEMS_DEAD_LETTER_TOPIC` | `notify-items.dlq` | Dead-letter topic |
| `PUBSUB_CONCURRENCY` | `10` | Messages the worker handles at once |
| `RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED` | `false` | Turn rate limits off |
| `RATE_LIMIT_DRY_RUN` | `false` | Count and log, never reject |
| `RATE_LIMIT_EXEMPT` | | Comma-separated `user:<id>`, `ip:<address>` or `ip:<CIDR>` |
| `LOG_LEVEL`, `LOG_FORMAT`, `LOG_SCHEMA`, `LOG_OUTPUT` | `info`, `json`, detected, stdout | See `github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/log` |
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` and other `OTEL_*` | | Traces are exported over OTLP when `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` (or `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT`) is set; metrics also need `OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp` |

## Subscriptions

Each consumer added with `zen add consumer` reads its own topic; its
variables start with `PUBSUB_<NAME>_` and are required.

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `PUBSUB_ORDER_EVENTS_TOPIC` | (required) | Topic of the order events consumer |
| `PUBSUB_ORDER_EVENTS_SUBSCRIPTION` | (required) | Its consumer group |
| `PUBSUB_ORDER_EVENTS_DEAD_LETTER_TOPIC` | (required) | Its dead-letter topic |
<!-- zen:subscriptions -->

## gRPC clients

Each service added with `zen add client` has its own variables, which
start with its name, for example `BILLING_`. Calls use TLS with the system
roots unless `<NAME>_INSECURE=true`.

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
<!-- zen:clients -->

## Production

- Set `APP_ENV=production`; unsafe settings such as `AUTH_DISABLED` are
  refused there.
- Secrets: and the credentials of
  telemetry exporters. Inject them from your secret store; never commit them.
- Create the topics, including the dead-letter topic, with your
  infrastructure tool, and keep `PUBSUB_TLS=true`.
- Set `TRUSTED_PROXIES` to the CIDRs of your load balancer, and keep
  `ADMIN_ADDR` off the public network.
